<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 13.55 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 13.55 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,823.6 billion levs on December 6 from 1,606 billion</p>
<p>levs a week earlier, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government rose 11.18 percent to 733 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 15.58 percent to 495.6</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms inched</p>
<p>up 0.52 percent to 135.2 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	  DEC 6-NOV29 NOV29-NOV1  NOV 1-SEPT27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	+13.55	+29.48	 +1.67</p>
<p> Credit to govt		 +11.18	+29.99	 +2.26</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	+15.58	+29.08	 +2.40</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms -0.52	 +2.36	 -1.94</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	 DEC 6	NOV 29	  NOV 1</p>
<p> Total internal credit	1,823.6     1,606.0	1,240.3</p>
<p> Credit to govt		   733.0	 659.3	  507.2</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	  495.6	 428.8	  332.2</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms  135.2	 134.5	  131.4</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms    1.09	  1.10	   1.12</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
